{"name":"Ice Climber","hex":"#25e2cd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ice climber","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who does ice climbing"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice_climber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice Climber","blocks":[{"text":"Ice Climber is a 1985 platform video game developed and published by Nintendo. It was released for both the arcade VS. System and the Famicom/Nintendo Entertainment System console. The main protagonists, Popo and Nana, collectively known as the Ice Climbers, scale 32 vertically scrolling, ice-covered mountains to recover stolen vegetables from a giant condor. In some European countries, Ice Climber was bundled with the Nintendo Entertainment System."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/IceClimberboxartnes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_Climber","wikidata":"Q1066657"},{"title":"Ice climbing","blocks":[{"text":"Ice climbing is a climbing discipline that involves ascending routes consisting entirely of frozen water. To ascend, the ice climber uses specialist equipment, particularly double ice axes and rigid crampons. To protect the route, the ice climber uses steel ice screws that require skill to employ safely and rely on the ice holding firm in any fall. Ice climbing routes can vary significantly by type, and include seasonally frozen waterfalls, high permanently frozen alpine couloirs, and large hanging icicles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Xaver_Bongard_in_der_Breitwangflue.jpg/330px-Xaver_Bongard_in_der_Breitwangflue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_climbing","wikidata":"Q1148495"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fd/NES_Ice_Climber.png/250px-NES_Ice_Climber.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/NES_Ice_Climber.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fd/NES_Ice_Climber.png/250px-NES_Ice_Climber.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Popo scales Mountain 1 surrounded by Topis and a Nitpicker.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANES_Ice_Climber.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Ice_Climbers_SSBU.png/250px-Ice_Climbers_SSBU.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Ice_Climbers_SSBU.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/12/Ice_Climbers_SSBU.png/250px-Ice_Climbers_SSBU.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Ice Climbers in Super Smash Bros. Ultimate.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIce_Climbers_SSBU.png"},{"srcset":"https://